{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Peoples will invoke the mountain.</b> For when they saw many peoples coming by sea, they would vow and volunteer of themselves out of fear of the sea, to go to Mount Zion to slaughter there sacrifices of righteousness, if they are delivered from the sea, as we say in חולין: 'each man' — this teaches that the gentiles vow vows and freewill offerings like Israel." "<b>For they will suck the abundance of the seas.</b> For in abundance the merchandise will come to them by way of the sea, and they profit." "<b>And hidden treasures of sand.</b> Like from the ships that break in the harbor and sink in the sea — they cast everything outside, and those who salvage the ship bury the money in the sand. And it says that even the ship and the money buried in the sand — they will find everything and take for themselves. And according to this plain sense, one may ask why Zebulun was placed before Issachar. But according to the midrash that they made a partnership — that Zebulun would engage in commerce and Issachar would engage in Torah — it works out well: ״rejoice, Zebulun, in your going out״ — on account of Issachar, who sits in your tents [engaged in Torah]."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:04.113287481Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}